 Thomson I'm just  wondering if you could describe the  different pieces of the music business  because you've got subscribers you've  got downloaders you got people by actual  physical music just run us through the  business there's six ways that people  consume music right now traditional  radio FM AM radio it's one way they can  the oldest way physical record sales CDs  and vinyl which as you know is growing  it over 50% a year downloads digital  downloads which is what Apple is the  magis iTunes and others but iTunes is  about eighty-five to ninety percent of  it worldwide  then there's streaming services and they  come in two different types ad supported  streaming services like YouTube and  Spotify free and VEVO and other ones  that are subscription which is Spotify  its domain also but Deezer is in there  in title and there are many more coming  online now so is Apple's new service  trying to do too much because it's  stitched together from its existing  service which includes the iTunes  download its two-year old internet radio  service and that hasn't having much of  an impact and also the beats  subscription music service it's a little  bit of everything as opposed to a simple  business model that say Pandora has or  that Deezer has or actually on the  contrary the reason why Apple has been  successful is because they've created an  ecosystem where people can live with  their music in every possible way they  can store it in their cloud they can  download if they want to download they  can listen to radio and now they can  stream the same way  Spotify will stream to and I disagree  that there will be disrupting Spotify or  any of the existing players there's a  big advantage to early movers in the  digital business in every business but  especially in digital I think that they  can tap they'll be launching on 800  million devices if they activate half of  them and they can convert at forty  percent which is how much Sirius XM  converts they have they have 